nothing goes with halloween like  halloween for more than 40 years when  the weather gets cold and the dark comes  early michael myers has returned to kill  again we're ranking every movie in the  halloween series from the 1978 original  to 2021's halloween kills  the greatest sin a movie can commit  especially a horror movie is to be  boring while other halloween sequels  have failed more spectacularly than this  one they at least deserve extra points  for ambition the return of michael myers  coasts on its own concept because it  does exactly what the title promises  bringing michael myers back and doing  almost nothing else  return picks up 10 years after the  original film finding michael as he  wakes from a decade-long coma and  overhears that he has a niece it doesn't  get much better from there in this movie  lori strode is revealed to have died in  a car accident leaving a young daughter  jaime michael meanders into town to find  her with his old nemesis dr sam loomis  in tow with the mystery of the original  halloween long gone the return of  michael myers turns into a tepid retread  of the first movie why watch halloween 4  when the original did everything better  the first time around  if halloween 4 disappoints by being too  safe the rob zombie remake went too far  in the opposite direction it was a bold  choice to hire a filmmaker with as  unique a vision as rob zombie to set a  new direction for the series  unfortunately the result is an  overcomplicated unpleasant mess stuck  halfway between reboot and prequel the  film dwells on the abusive childhood  that warped young michael myers mind  before leaping forward in time to once  again recreate the original movie the  result is a film that's relentlessly  dreary and structurally unsound rob  zombie is definitely a director with  style but when it comes to his  filmography this is no slam dunk it's  certainly not a slam in the back of your  dragula  the curse of michael myers is so  compromised that fans would go on to  circulate an early work print version  labeled a producer's cut as a bootleg  for nearly 20 years before it was  officially released in fact the writer  of the movie revealed in a fangoria  interview that the curse of the title  started as a joke about the nightmarish  process of making the film this 1995  entry finds jaime escaping from a cult  with a newborn baby six years after she  and her unkillable uncle michael were  abducted by a mysterious man in black at  the end of halloween five michael chases  her down and kills her but her baby  lives and winds up in the care of tommy  doyle played by paul rudd in one of his  earliest movie roles tommy has been  obsessed with myers ever since surviving  the events of the original film and he  teams up with dr loomis to protect the  newborn the plot that unfolds reveals  the secrets of the cult of thorn a  druidic order bent on cultivating power  through human sacrifice their leader is  the man in black who is revealed to be  dr terence wynn a character who appeared  in one scene of the original halloween  that you almost certainly won't remember  this tangled drama leaves little room  for either scares or fun meaning the  most compelling reason to watch is to  marvel at how little paul rudd has aged  in over a quarter century i don't really  believe in age or numbers you know i  don't  the halloween series has a track record  of taking absurd sequel concepts and  taking them too seriously there may be  no better example of this problem than  2002's halloween resurrection the eighth  entry in the franchise begins as a  satire of reality tv with a webcast show  called dangertainment locking  contestants into the old myers house for  a night of scares  [Music]  the hosts played by tyra banks and busta  rhymes have prepared a number of spooky  traps for the players but the  dangertainment gets real when michael  comes home the first victim sadly is the  cleverness of this setup the movie  quickly devolves into an unmemorable  romp through dark rooms far from  resurrecting the halloween franchise  this movie puts the series in the ground  it also features a depressing cameo from  jamie lee curtis as laurie strode she  appears in the beginning of the movie  locked up in a mental hospital where  she's killed by michael myers in the  first 15 minutes  rob zombie returned to write and direct  his own take on a halloween sequel and  it was a marked improvement over his  first attempt no longer bound by the  obligation to remake john carpenter's  original zombies halloween 2 cuts loose  for a unique story examining the effects  of the previous film's traumas on its  characters loomis was trying to sell his  new book lori was plagued by intrusive  killer impulses while michael dealt with  surreal visions of his mother zombie  chose to shoot halloween 2 on 16  millimeter film lending it an  authentically gritty grindhouse feel  that set it apart from most modern  horror movies this decision played to  the movie strengths namely its  strikingly surreal hallucinatory imagery  while more psychologically interesting  than many other entries in the series  its big ideas are sadly buried beneath  uninspired violence and an unrelentingly  grim tone  what the fifth halloween may lack in  originality it makes up for with sheer  trashy horror movie fun this time jamie  lloyd has been left traumatized by the  horror she faced one year earlier she's  experiencing hallucinations that suggest  some kind of telepathic link with her  uncle michael who vanished down a mine  shaft at the end of halloween four the  real joy of revenge is in donald  pleasance's fourth turn as dr loomis who  gets more and more over the top in his  desperation to convince authorities that  myers is alive pure evil and coming back  to kill once more he spends about as  much time in this movie terrorizing  jaime as michael myers does  what do you think he's going to do with  that  the appeal of this film's teen cast is  unmatched by any other halloween film  besides the original decked out in late  80s fashion and talking about how love  makes your heart feel like it's made of  neon jaime's climactic flight through a  laundry chute to escape her uncle's  knife has more genuine tension than many  of the other sequel's kill sequences  combined it also gave audiences one of  the most bonkers moments in the series  in which loomis traps michael in a net  and beats him with a 2x4  john carpenter has always seemed to hold  mixed feelings about the halloween  series he said in a 2014 interview with  deadline michael myers was an absence of  character and yet all the sequels are  trying to explain that that's silliness  carpenter turned down the opportunity to  direct halloween too but agreed to help  write it in the interest of maintaining  some share in the phenomenon he had  helped create the result is a film that  continues the story of halloween as  directly as possible while still putting  in an effort to feel different to that  end halloween two ratchets up the gore  factor in the style of the then new  slashers like friday the 13th picking up  in the final scene of its predecessor  the sequel is set entirely on the very  same night letting myers loose in a  hospital in search of lorry with dr  loomis in pursuit meanwhile michael's  motivations are explored revealing for  the first time the family connection  between lori and michael that would go  on to define so many of the sequels in  the end halloween 2 is a movie that  believes it shouldn't exist but still  gives a valiant effort to give viewers a  good time it's not perfect but it's  something as carpenter candidly told  deadline i had to write the second movie  and every night i sat there and wrote  with a six pack of beer trying to get  through this thing and i didn't do a  very good job but  that was it  halloween h2o is undoubtedly one of the  silliest titles in horror history the  movie isn't even about water the title  refers to the 20 years that have passed  since the first two halloween movies  lori strode is revealed to be living  under an assumed name after faking her  death serving as headmistress of a  private school attended by her teenage  son john is it weird kinda but it's fun  what the [ __ ] do you think you're doing  mom i'm really uncomfortable with you  saying that well then don't put me in  the position john h2o is very much a  halloween for the scream generation with  extremely strong late 90s vibes from  josh hartnett to ll cool j to the creed  song that plays over the closing credits  despite all that h2o is a surprisingly  tight slick thriller that lets laurie  fight back when michael comes for her  son it's jamie lee curtis who makes h2o  worth watching not only is her  performance as a still-haunted  middle-aged lori compelling but the  story was her idea she recalled in an  interview with the los angeles times  that was how i pitched the movie  regaining the soul by facing your own  fear when the stalky becomes the stalker  i guarantee you the audience will go  crazy  after years away from the big screen  michael myers once again rose from the  dead in 2017 it was announced that  blumhouse productions had hired david  gordon green and danny mcbride to  reinvigorate the franchise for a new  generation the result was jamie lee  curtis's iconic lori strode being  reinvented once again as a survivor  turned survivalist this time when  michael came back to haddenfield the  final girl would be ready audiences  responded well to the end result which  ignored all the other sequels entirely  the result was the highest grossing  halloween film ever made up to that  point making for an undeniable  crowd-pleasing revival of the classic  horror series  gotcha  if 2018's halloween was the spark then  halloween kills is a raging fire this  action-packed movie brings the town of  haddonfield together with the survivors  of michael myers teaming up to finish  off michael myers once and for all it's  a gory and intense escalation of  everything the first movie in the  revival trilogy promised setting things  up for a conclusion in the planned  sequel halloween ends if you love the  halloween films you'll love how  halloween kills commits to fanservice  without betraying what made the 2018  movie work much like the original two  halloween films these new movies both  take place right after the other and  taken together they feel like one long  masterful exercise in escalating horror  the boldest thing attempted by any of  the halloween sequels is to not be a  halloween sequel the third movie tried  to pivot the franchise into being an  anthology series telling an entirely new  story about a different halloween night  the movie is actually about an ancient  order of warlocks but season of the  warlock doesn't have the same ring to it  it's centered around a company cult that  aims to slaughter children on a massive  scale with a crop of cursed halloween  masks the goal to get revenge against  america for the commercialization of  halloween and usher in a new age of  witchcraft despite being disliked at the  time of its release season of the witch  is full of clever and memorable moments  unfortunately it was subjected to a  disappointing box office and scathing  reviews from fans and critics and the  intriguing anthology concept was  abandoned  any list arranging the halloween films  from worst to best is doomed to be  anti-climactic because there's only one  way for it to end the merits of every  sequel and reboot can be debated but  there's no denying that the original is  in a class of its own no hot takes here  the best halloween movie is 1978's  halloween halloween became legendary  because it's elemental its teen  characters are charmingly ordinary there  are no contrived plot twists or  convoluted motivations behind michael  myers he's just a man in a mask who  wants to kill everyone he sees the  tension hovering over the movie steadily  builds until the killing spree begins  and it doesn't let up until the movie  ends with michael vanishing into the  night doomed to haunt your nightmares  for the rest of your days it's a  minimalist masterpiece that redefined a  genre by reminding audiences that all  you need  is one good scare you know it's  halloween i guess everyone's entitled  one good scare  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite horror movies are coming  soon subscribe to our youtube channel  and hit the bell so you don't miss a  single one  [Music]

